From: openrc2 ASan rollout (Hunt-Subagent, verifiziert im Gast)
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] free child-private memory before exit (procsub, exec-fail)

Zwei Stellen, an denen sterbende Kinder Allokationen zuruecklassen, die LSan
meldet und den Exit-Status kipppt (127->1 bei exec-fail):
- subst.c: procsub-Kind gibt sein privates pathname frei (Parent hat eigene Kopie).
- execute_cmd.c: exec-fail-Pfad gibt args/command vor exit() frei.

--- a/subst.c
+++ b/subst.c
@@ -6580,4 +6580,8 @@
   dev_fd_list[parent_pipe_fd] = 0;
 #endif /* HAVE_DEV_FD */

+  /* The parent keeps its own copy of PATHNAME for the expansion result. This copy is private to the child and is no longer needed: the filename was already consumed above. Free it now so a leak checker does not report it as orphaned when this child exits. */
+  free (pathname);
+  pathname = (char *)NULL;
+
   /* subshells shouldn't have this flag, which controls using the temporary
--- a/execute_cmd.c
+++ b/execute_cmd.c
@@ -5929,5 +5929,9 @@
 	 type it in. */
       args = strvec_from_word_list (words, 0, 0, (int *)NULL);
-      exit (shell_execve (command, args, export_env));
+      /* shell_execve only returns if the exec fails. Free the argument vector before exiting: leaving it allocated makes leak checkers report it and clobber the exit status we are about to return. */
+      result = shell_execve (command, args, export_env);
+      free (args);
+      free (command);
+      exit (result);
     }
   else
